\caption(All twelve derivatives match the analytic result. Stable pixel NLL also remains finite for logits ±100, and the standard-normal posterior has exactly zero KL.)
\alttext(Two straight lines pass through latent coordinate 0.2 at zero noise. Doubling the posterior standard deviation doubles the slope.)

> Native data preparation and the complete experiment

The native mnist-assets task supplies label-balanced 1,000/200/200 fit/validation/test pools
and source manifests. Fit and validation are disjoint records of the training IDX file;
test IDs address the separate official test IDX file. Images are thresholded once at
normalized intensity >=0.5, equivalent to raw uint8 >=128. These tiny pools and this static
threshold do not constitute the official binarized-MNIST benchmark protocol. Labels only
choose diagnostic gallery rows and colour the latent scatter; they never enter fitting.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n                       = dm::nn;
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", cache.string());
  const auto pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(cache / "saliency");
  std::print("| pool | records | geometry | binary foreground fraction |\n|---|---:|---|---:|\n");
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const auto x = n::cast(n::greater_equal(pools[k].images, .5), n::DType::Float64);
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | 28x28x1 | {:.6f} |\n",
        k == 0   ? "fit"
        : k == 1 ? "validation"
                 : "test",
        x.size(0),
        n::mean(x).item());
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
