\caption(Epoch 3 wins validation. Test reconstruction NLL is 196.893673820 nats, analytic KL is 8.613429453, and their sum is 205.507103273. The fitting-only binary mean is a separate MSE reference.)

All 16 archives, 8,817,594 array values, complete batch history and CSV/TSV files reproduce
the original source exactly. The report replaces one host MSE sum with a tensor Float64
reduction: mean_decode_test_mse differs by 2.998e-15. All other non-timing JSON values remain
exact. Fixed-noise repeats, single/batch inference, target-free decoder equality and parameter
immutability are checked before saving results.

> Validation measures a completed epoch

The training trace is a record-weighted mean of pre-update minibatch objectives, each with
its own current parameters and one noise draw. Validation uses the completed epoch's fixed
parameters and four fixed draws. Their separation therefore does not by itself diagnose
an overfitting gap.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vanilla_vae_validation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream input("build/vanilla_vae/history.tsv");
  std::string   header;
  std::getline(input, header);
  std::vector<double> epochs, train, validation;
  double              e, t, n, k, v;
  while (input >> e >> t >> n >> k >> v) {
    epochs.push_back(e);
    train.push_back(t);
    validation.push_back(v);
  }
  if (epochs.size() != 3)
    return 1;
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(epochs, train, "train (pre)", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(epochs, train, "", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .lines(epochs, validation, "validation (end)", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .points(epochs, validation, "", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .title("Negative ELBO estimates / distinct observation times")
      .x_label("completed epoch / all three eligible")
      .y_label("NLL plus KL / nats per image")
      .x_ticks({1, 2, 3}, {"1", "2", "3"})
      .save_svg("build/vanilla_vae_validation.svg");
}
