> Decode independent prior codes without the encoder

Only the four decoder leaves are restored below. Twenty standard-normal codes from seed
1997 produce exactly the previously saved prior probabilities. No image, encoder or label
is needed. All twenty outputs are shown in draw order, without rejection or quality ranking.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vanilla_vae_priors.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto     arrays = n::load_npz("build/vanilla_vae/model_arrays.npz"),
             prior      = n::load_npz("build/vanilla_vae/prior.npz");
  auto find             = [](const n::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  n::ParameterStore decoder(1951);
  n::models::GaussianVaeDecode(decoder, n::zeros({1, 2}), 784, 2, 64);
  for (const auto& name : decoder.names())
    decoder.set(name, find(arrays, name));
  if (decoder.size() != 4)
    return 1;
  const auto probability =
      n::sigmoid(n::models::GaussianVaeDecode(decoder, find(prior, "z"), 784, 2, 64));
  if (!n::equal_bits(probability, find(prior, "probability")))
    return 1;
  n::save_image_grid(
      probability.reshape({20, 28, 28, 1}),
      "build/vanilla_vae_priors.png",
      5,
      0,
      1,
      4,
      220. / 255.,
      4);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/vanilla_vae_priors.png)
// result_end

\caption(All twenty unfiltered prior decoder probability images, five per row. Some outputs are ambiguous; this short fit is not a generation-quality benchmark.)
\alttext(Twenty smooth, sometimes ambiguous digit-like probability images are displayed in their original prior draw order.)

A separate 9×9 grid decodes **Cartesian coordinates**, not Gaussian quantiles: coordinate 1
runs -2 to 2 left to right and coordinate 2 runs 2 to -2 top to bottom, both in steps of 0.5.
Equal spatial steps do not represent equal prior probability. This view describes the learned
decoder surface and cannot establish semantic coordinate control.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vanilla_vae_grid.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto     arrays = n::load_npz("build/vanilla_vae/model_arrays.npz"),
             prior      = n::load_npz("build/vanilla_vae/prior.npz");
  auto find             = [](const n::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  const auto z = find(prior, "grid_z");
  for (int r = 0; r < 9; ++r)
    for (int c = 0; c < 9; ++c)
      if (z.at({r * 9 + c, 0}) != -2. + .5 * c || z.at({r * 9 + c, 1}) != 2. - .5 * r)
        return 1;
  n::ParameterStore decoder(1951);
  n::models::GaussianVaeDecode(decoder, n::zeros({1, 2}), 784, 2, 64);
  for (const auto& name : decoder.names())
    decoder.set(name, find(arrays, name));
  const auto probability = n::sigmoid(n::models::GaussianVaeDecode(decoder, z, 784, 2, 64));
  if (!n::equal_bits(probability, find(prior, "grid_probability")))
    return 1;
  n::save_image_grid(
      probability.reshape({81, 28, 28, 1}),
      "build/vanilla_vae_grid.png",
      9,
      0,
      1,
      4,
      220. / 255.,
      3);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/vanilla_vae_grid.png)
// result_end

\caption(Cartesian decoder grid: x=-2…2 left to right, y=2…-2 top to bottom, spacing 0.5 in each coordinate. All 81 saved probabilities are verified by code-only decoding before plotting.)
\alttext(A nine-by-nine grid of probability images shows smooth decoder changes across a regular two-dimensional code lattice.)

> Evidence and limits

The native Gaussian core supplies reparameterization, analytic KL, stable Bernoulli NLL and
the full dense model. The old eight-field compatibility record forwards to that same core;
its signature stays available for remaining consumers. Source arrays and histories agree
exactly, and the independent NumPy development check verifies all 101,652 first derivatives,
the bit-exact first Adam step, explicit Gaussian draws, saved forwards, all eligible
validation candidates and target-free prior decoding. It never trains or prepares data:

```
python3 scripts/check_variational_autoencoder.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.2_variational_autoencoders/build/vanilla_vae
```

The run demonstrates a differentiable stochastic bottleneck and reproducible prior decoding.
Its small balanced pools, three training epochs and qualitative figures do not establish
benchmark likelihood, realistic generation, disentanglement or generalization to other data.
